    "houses": {"obj-houses": [9, 16]},
    "closed": 0,
    "opening": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4],
    "closing": [4, 3, 5, 6, 7, 0],
    "fps": 14,
    "range": 26,
    "closeAfter": 1.2
  },
  "rooms": {
    "about": "Rooms inside houses (world/rooms/*.json). 'void' is the colour around a room. Each style names the picture sheet and which of its 16 px pieces make the floor, the doorway and each part of the walls. A room's map is a box: 'W' walls (the top two rows are the back wall), '_' floor; its 'exit' is a '_' gap in the bottom wall. A style with \"shape\": \"cave\" draws any shape instead (Rooms.drawCave): rock with floor below shows its stone 'front', other rock its dark top; 'top' is where the 4 x 4 block of rock tops starts in the 'tex' sheet (columns: open left / both sides rock / open right / both open; rows the same for up and down); pieces are [column, row]; 'floor' pieces are mixed by place, with a 'floorRare' one every 'rareEvery' tiles or so.",
